# Commit messages

Use this format for every git commit in this repo:

```
[edit-type] detailed edit
```

- **edit-type**: scope or kind of change (lowercase). Examples from this project: `frontend`, `feature`, `fix`, `test`, `data`, `db`, `refactor`, `chore`, `cleanup`, `txt`. Combine when needed, e.g. `[feature/fix]`.
- **detailed edit**: one short sentence describing why or what changed (lowercase start is fine).

Examples:

```
[frontend] pe-db exportation
[test] add system test for evaluation
[feature] connect pe-db to pe-ensemble, sync up pytorch versions
[feature/fix] deeppe standardization and exportation, fix pridict1 endo exportation
```

Do not use generic messages like "update files" or "misc changes".
